
  This feature ensures the last 4 digits of the invoice_number column in the d_product_revenue_clone table (replica of d_product_revenue) are masked using ‘*’, meeting compliance requirements for customer information protection.

  Background:
    Given Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks"
    And Unity Catalog Schema is "purgo_playground"
    And source table is "purgo_databricks.purgo_playground.d_product_revenue"
    And destination table is "purgo_databricks.purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone"
    And user has write permissions on both tables
    And environment is Databricks with PySpark version compatible with masking logic
    And the d_product_revenue table has a column invoice_number with String or Numeric data type

  Scenario: Drop and create clone of d_product_revenue table
    Given the table d_product_revenue_clone exists
    When the table d_product_revenue_clone is dropped
    Then no table named d_product_revenue_clone should exist in schema purgo_playground
    When a clone of d_product_revenue is created as d_product_revenue_clone
    Then d_product_revenue_clone should exist with identical schema as d_product_revenue

  Scenario Outline: Mask last 4 digits of invoice_number with ‘*’
    Given d_product_revenue_clone contains the following invoice_number values:
      | invoice_number |
      | <original_invoice_number> |
    When the masking process is executed on invoice_number column
    Then the stored invoice_number should be "<masked_invoice_number>"

    Examples:
      | original_invoice_number | masked_invoice_number |
      | 1234234534             | 123423****           |
      | 987654321098           | 98765432****         |
      | AB12345678             | AB1234****           |
      | 8765                   | ****                 |
      | 543                    | ***                  |
      | XY12                   | ****                 |
      | 1                      | *                    |
      | 000012340000           | 00001234****         |
      | 12AB34XY56             | 12AB34XY**           |

  Scenario Outline: Error handling for null or invalid invoice_number values
    Given d_product_revenue_clone contains the following invoice_number:
      | invoice_number |
      | <invalid_invoice_number> |
    When the masking process is executed on invoice_number column
    Then the following error condition should be triggered with message "<error_message>"

    Examples:
      | invalid_invoice_number | error_message                               |
      | NULL                  | "invoice_number is NULL: cannot mask value" |
      |                      | "invoice_number is empty: cannot mask value" |
      | @#$%^&*()            | "invoice_number contains only special characters: masking all as *"|

  Scenario Outline: Validation rules for masking invoice_number
    Given an invoice_number value <test_value>
    When the masking logic is applied
    Then the result should satisfy the following rules:
      | rule_description                                   |
      | If length >= 4, mask last 4 chars as '*'           |
      | If length < 4, mask all chars as '*'               |
      | If value contains alphanumeric or numeric, mask chars only, preserve format |
      | If value is NULL or empty, do not mask, set to error or log error    |

    Examples:
      | test_value          |
      | 123456789          |
      | AB1234CD           |
      | 123                |
      |                    |
      | NULL               |
      | A                  |
      | 1234               |
      | ABCD               |

  Scenario: Ensure masked invoice_number format is preserved and no data loss
    Given d_product_revenue_clone table has invoice_number values before masking
    When the masking logic is run
    Then all other columns should remain unchanged
    And only the last 4 characters of invoice_number are replaced with '*'
    And all invoice_number field lengths remain unchanged

  Scenario: Logging and auditing of masking process
    Given the masking process is initiated
    When a value is masked or an error occurs
    Then an entry is added to the audit log with timestamp, original value, masked value (if masked), and error message (if error occurs)

  Scenario: Masking should be idempotent
    Given an invoice_number value already masked (last 4 are '*')
    When the masking logic runs again
    Then the invoice_number remains unchanged
    And no additional masking is applied

  Scenario Outline: Masking on edge case inputs
    Given the following invoice_number test case: <edge_case_value>
    When the masking process is executed
    Then the resulting invoice_number is <edge_case_result>
    And any relevant error/warning is <edge_case_error>

    Examples:
      | edge_case_value | edge_case_result | edge_case_error                            |
      | 12              | **               |                                            |
      |                 |                  | "invoice_number is empty: cannot mask value"|
      | NULL            |                  | "invoice_number is NULL: cannot mask value" |
      | ****            | ****             |                                            |
      |   1234          |   ****           |                                            |